QuestGuidance.Register("en",213,{
[6785]="7003E291\n1\tTalk to Aragorn on the road through the mysterious wood\tAragorn has turned back to hear your opinion of the mysterious wood through which the company now travels.\n2\tTalk to Legolas on the road through the mysterious wood\tLegolas has dismounted and is staring into the trees.\n3\tTalk to Théoden on the road through the mysterious wood\tThéoden is on the road through the mysterious wood. He has never seen Ents before, and the sight has filled him with wonder.\n4\tTalk to Gandalf on the road through the mysterious wood\tGandalf is on the road, waiting to proceed.\n5\tJourney with the company beyond the Fords of Isen\tThe company continues toward Isengard.\n6\tTalk to Aragorn beyond the Fords of Isen\tAragorn has slowed beyond the Fords. He wishes to speak with you.\n7\tTalk to Éomer on the road\tÉomer has heard a horseman approaching, and wants to speak with you.\n8\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad and the Grey Company have accomplished their mission, and Halbarad wants to speak with you.\n9\tTalk to Golodir\030Talk to Calenglad\030Talk to Radanir\030Talk to Corunir\tMany of your friends among the Grey Company wish to speak with you before continuing on.\n10\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn is speaking with Halbarad past the Fords of Isen.\n",
[6786]="70009F3B\n1\tTalk to the Ranger protector standing before you\tSpeak with the Ranger protector before you search for Amarthiel.\n2\tFind and stop Amarthiel\tFind Amarthiel and discover her plans.\n3\tDefeat Morguldur\tYou must defeat the Black Númenórean.\n",
[6787]="7005471F\n1\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas would like to return to Echad Taerdim. You should talk to Legolas.\n2\tTravel to Echad Taerdim with Legolas and Atli\tLegolas would like to return to Echad Taerdim. You should travel with Legolas and Atli to the Ranger camp.\n3\tDefend the camp\tStrange uruks are attacking the Ranger camp. Defend the camp!\n4\tListen to Rûkhor\tThe uruks have fallen back, but a strange man has appeared above the camp. You should listen to Rûkhor.\n5\tTalk to Mablung\tThe attack has been repelled. You should talk to Mablung.\n",
[6788]="70071BC0\n1\tTalk to Nabatínu\tYou should talk to Nabatínu when you are ready to begin the assault.\n2\tTalk to Nabatínu\tYour company has defeated the Ordâkhai defending the supply caravan. You should talk to Nabatínu about what to do next.\n3\tCollect supply crates (total: 6)\tNabatínu has given orders to everyone in your company. You should collect the supply crates.\n4\tTalk to Rhadrog\tYou have collected the supply crates. You should talk to Rhadrog about what to do next.\n",
[6789]="7006B5DB\n1\tTalk to Balakhâd\tBalakhâd has more to tell you.\n2\tListen to Balakhâd's account\tListen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.\n3\tTalk to Balakhâd\tBalakhâd has more to tell you.\n4\tListen to Balakhâd's account\tListen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.\n5\tTalk to Balakhâd\tBalakhâd has more to tell you.\n6\tListen to Balakhâd's account\tListen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.\n7\tTalk to Balakhâd\tBalakhâd has more to tell you.\n8\tListen to Balakhâd's account\tListen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.\n",
[6790]="70060584\n1\tTalk to Cariad\tYou should talk to Cariad before approaching Erlys.\n2\tObserve the discussion\tCariad wishes to discuss matters with Erlys.\n3\tConfront the spy outside\tA spy of Saruman's has been spotted outside the cave. Erlys has ordered you to confront and defeat the spy.\n4\tWait and stand your ground\tIgrain has offered to let you leave so that she may freely spy on the Cuan-lûth refugees. You should wait and stand your ground.\n5\tDefeat Igrain\tDefeating Igrain may help the Cuan-lûth trust you more.\n6\tObserve Igrain's interrogation\tIgrain has surrendered. You should observe her interrogation.\n7\tTalk to Cariad\tYou should talk to Cariad about Erlys' opinion of the Rangers.\n",
[6791]="70071D92\n1\tJoin Mizâdi and Numûru outside the council chambers\tJoin Mizâdi and Numûru outside the council chambers.\n2\tEnter the council chamber with Mizâdi within the Shorakhúna\tEnter the council chamber with Mizâdi within the Shorakhúna.\n3\tListen to the conversation between the Doorwards and Mizâdi\tListen to the conversation between the Doorwards and Mizâdi.\n4\tPick up the sword from the table in the Shorakhúna\tPick up the sword from the table in the Shorakhúna.\n5\tPlace the sword on the table in front of Sarâgh, Master of Spears\tPlace the sword on the table in front of Sarâgh, Master of Spears.\n6\tListen to the conversation between the Doorwards and Mizâdi\tListen to the conversation between the Doorwards and Mizâdi.\n7\tListen to the conversation between the Doorwards and Mizâdi\tListen to the conversation between the Doorwards and Mizâdi.\n8\tSpeak with Numûru inside the Shorakhúna\tSpeak with Numûru inside the Shorakhúna.\n9\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside the Shorakhúna\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside the Shorakhúna.\n10\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the Doorwards\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the Doorwards.\n11\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the Doorwards\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the Doorwards.\n",
[6792]="7006AFDB\n1\tTalk to Rothog\tRothog has summoned you to his chambers to hear a specific complaint from one of his nobles regarding one of the gladiators.\n2\tSpeak to Zarzíra and witness the proceedings\tApproach Zarzíra Dawn-star to begin her petition.\n3\tSpeak to Rothog the Storm\tSpeak to Rothog regarding Zarzíra Dawn-star's petition\n",
[6793]="70056E92\n1\tTalk to Glóin\tGlóin stands among the warriors of the Longbeard army before the Anvil of Winterstith.\n2\tListen to the questions of the Longbeards\tGlóin and the warriors of the Longbeard army marvel at Durin's secret departure from Skarháld.\n3\tCarefully approach Durin\tGlóin is worried for the prince of the Longbeards, and has asked you to slowly approach Durin and learn why he came to Winterstith.\n4\tListen to Heilar's account\tDurin stares into the sheet of ice at Winterstith, muttering quietly.\n5\tGently break Durin's reverie, if you can\tDurin stares into the sheet of ice at Winterstith, muttering quietly.\n6\tTalk to Durin\tYou have managed to break Durin's reverie at the Anvil of Winterstith, but he still speaks slowly, as if waking from a deep sleep.\n7\tListen to Durin as he addresses the great force of Longbeards\tDurin has managed to shake free of his reverie, seeing for the first time the Longbeard army from the Lonely Mountain.\n8\tTalk to Mírkuz\tThe Zhélruka Mírkuz followed on the heels of the Longbeard army during its march from Skarháld, and now he has interrupted Durin's speech.\n9\tListen to Durin as he addresses the great force of Longbeards\tNewly-resolved, Durin addresses the Longbeard army before the Anvil of Winterstith.\n10\tTalk to Mírkuz\tMírkuz has listened to the words of Durin with growing displeasure and worry, and now he wishes to voice his concerns to you.\n",
[6794]="70021E86\n1\tTalk to Frithgeir\tFrithgeir is working to prepare the brew for Nár so you may speak to him without difficulty.\n2\tTalk to Corunir\030Talk to Elladan\030Talk to Calenglad\tFrithgeir is preparing the brew for Nár and has recommended that while you wait you speak with the members of the Grey Company who have come to Zudrugund.\n3\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad wishes to speak with you while Frithgeir prepares the brew for Nár.\n4\tLearn what Nona wants from the dwarves\tNona has burst into the dwarf-hall, intending to confront the dwarves about the fate of her brother Wadu.\n5\tTalk to Nona\tNona has demanded an explanation from you.\n6\tListen to the exchange between Nona and Nár\tFrithgeir has prepared the brew for Nár, and you should now see if it has the promised effect.\n7\tTalk to Nár\tNár seems to be more aware of his surroundings, thanks to the brew supplied by Frithgeir, and may now tell you what he said to Wadu.\n8\tTalk to Nár\tNár has offered to take you to the mines below Zudrugund, where he last remembers seeing Wadu. Perhaps the mystery of what happened to Nona's brother here remains below.\n9\tTalk to Elladan\tYou have travelled deep into the mine beneath Zudrugund with Nár, Elladan, and Nona. Elladan has had a curious feeling that you have been watched for some time now.\n10\tTalk to Nona\tNona wears a puzzled expression. She seems dissatisfied with the journey and wishes to speak with you.\n11\tTalk to Elladan\tElladan is thinking, pondering what to do next, now that you are deep beneath Zudrugund and Nár is passing out of awareness again.\n12\tFind and use the lever that unlocks the gate\tA locked gate blocks further progress into the mine, and Elladan has asked you to find the lever that should open it.\n13\tRejoin Elladan, Nona, and Nár below\tYou have pulled the lever to open the gate and should now rejoin your friends below.\n14\tTalk to Elladan\tYour friends are missing. Have they already gone on past the gate that blocked passage deeper into the mine?\n15\tFollow Elladan to Nár and listen to the dwarf's tale\tYour friends are deep within the mine, seeking the truth of what befell Wadu in the depths when he came here with Nár.\n16\tTalk to Nona\tNona has learned the truth: that her brother Wadu found his courage far below Zudrugund and defeated a mighty gwiber in the depths.\n17\tTalk to Elladan\tElladan is waiting to speak with you about Nár's mysterious and sudden change.\n",
[6795]="7001792C\n1\tTalk to Techeryn\tTecheryn is standing on the path that winds up to the summit of Weathertop. Techeryn is waiting to speak with you.\n2\tPlace rune-stones on flat stones upon Weathertop's summit (total: 3)\tThree flat stones can be found on the summit of Weathertop. Techeryn has asked you to place three rune-stones on flat stones on the summit of Weathertop, and to wait for each of them to be struck by lightning.\n3\tWait for lightning to strike all three of the rune-stones\tTecheryn has assured you that lightning will strike all three of the rune-stones you have placed on the summit of Weathertop, and you are not to return to her until it does.\n4\tCollect rune-stones (total: 3)\tLightning has struck each of the three rune-stones you placed on the summit, and you should now collect them all again.\n5\tBring rune-stones to Techeryn\tTecheryn has come to the summit of Weathertop, and is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[6796]="7004CE99\n1\tInvestigate the camp\tYou should investigate the refugee camp where the incident was said to have occurred.\n2\tYou should investigate the refugee camp where the incident was said to have occurred.\t\n3\tReturn to investigating\tYou should return to the centre of the refugee camp.\n4\tGo east of the camp\tYou should investigate the sounds coming from east of the camp.\n5\tDefend yourself\tYou should defend yourself from the Easterling attackers.\n6\tTalk to Enkárvo\tYou should talk to Enkárvo, the young Dorwinion man you met in Dale.\n",
[6797]="7002CDA4\n1\tExplore the ruins under Ost Celebrant\tDoron hopes to find the Easterling invader among the crumbling tunnels of Ost Celebrant. Explore the ruins and try to uncover his whereabouts.\n2\tSearch the ruins for the Easterling\tYou have uncovered a room decorated with strange banners and trinkets that fill you with dread. While you do not see the Easterling, you believe him to be nearby.\n3\tDefeat Maraz\tThe Easterling, Maraz, has revealed that he drove the brigands into serving his brotherhood, and that he and his people seek to crush Rohan beginning with Parth Celebrant. He must be defeated before his plans can come to fruition.\n4\tTalk to Doron\tDoron can be called to your side with the horn you carry.\n",
[6798]="7004E1E2\n1\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III is at Ravenhill. You have come to Ravenhill with King Thorin III and should now seek an audience with Dís.\n2\tFollow King Thorin III into Ravenhill\tKing Thorin III is at Ravenhill. Hoping to answer an urgent summons, King Thorin III has travelled to Ravenhill. You should follow him.\n3\tTalk to Dís at Ravenhill\tDís can be found in the chambers of Ravenhill. You have come to Ravenhill seeking to answer an urgent summons. You should talk to Dís.\n4\tListen to King Thorin III and Arcah\tKing Thorin III is speaking with Arcah, Daughter of Croär, chief of the ravens of Ravenhill.\n5\tTalk to Arcah, Daughter of Croär\tArcah, Daughter of Croär, is at Ravenhill. After speaking with the King under the Mountain, Arcah desires to learn more of you.\n6\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III is at Ravenhill. You have spoken to Arcah and told her much of your adventures, and you should now speak to King Thorin III.\n",
[6799]="7000D7A3\n1\tFind Bethad in Ologfil\tThe hillman Bethad must be somewhere in this foetid cave - whether he could possibly be alive or not is anyone's guess.\n2\tDefeat Ulkrank\tBethad has been imprisoned by the gorthorog war-leader Ulkrank, who must be slain before the scout can be safely freed.\n3\tFree Bethad from his imprisonment\tWith the death of Ulkrank, you should be able to free Bethad from his prison and escape from the dark lair of Ologfil.\n",
[6800]="700649F5\n1\tTalk to Crannog\tCrannog can be found at Fail-á-Khro. You have followed Crannog and the Trév Gállorg to Fail-á-Khro to parley with the Trév Duvárdain. You should talk to Crannog.\n2\tListen as Crannog addresses the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain\tThe Trév Gállorg have gathered to Fail-á-Khro to parley with the Trév Duvárdain. You should listen as Crannog addresses the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain.\n3\tWitness the parley at Fail-á-Khro\tThe Trév Gállorg have gathered to Fail-á-Khro to parley with the Trév Duvárdain. You should witness the parley between the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain.\n4\tTalk to Crannog\tCrannog can be found at Fail-á-Khro. The parley has concluded. You should talk to Crannog.\n",
[6801]="700216AC\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad is waiting to speak with you outside the ring-forges.\n2\tTalk to Fúsi Gem-cutter\tFúsi Gem-cutter has emerged from the ring-forges with a request for you.\n3\tPick up a treasure-coffer from the corner of the room where they are stored\tTreasure-coffers from Minas Elendúr can be found in the corner of the ruins. Fúsi Gem-cutter has asked you to bring him more gold from the coffers you retrieved from Minas Elendúr.\n4\tTalk to Candaith\tCandaith has asked to speak with you, if you have a moment to spare.\n5\tTalk to Elrohir\tElrohir is waiting for you in the courtyard north of Candaith and Halbarad.\n6\tInvestigate the distant shout\tA distant shout has broken the stillness. What has happened?\n7\tWhat danger has come to the ring-forges, and what does it signify for the Grey Company?\t\n8\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir has remained at the entrance courtyard of the ring-forges in order to delay the attacking uruks. He needs your help.\n9\tTalk to Halbarad\tThe uruks have been defeated and the plans of the Grey Company remain intact.\n",
[6802]="7006D5AE\n1\tSpeak with Ashâmi to begin the hunt\tAshâmi appears a bit shaken as she looks over the woods. You, too, have an uneasy feeling in these woods.\n2\tSpeak with Ashâmi to continue the hunt for Kanagir\tThere has been no sign of the serval Numûru described to Ashâmi. The woods are eerily still and quiet.\n3\tSpeak with Ashâmi to continue the hunt for Kanagir\tAshâmi stopped her search and looked back into the woods. Something still feels off.\n4\tSpeak with Ashâmi about how to proceed\tAshâmi looks shaken, but resolute. The serval pack attacked without warning. The serval Kanagir, as described, was not among them. You feel like you are being stalked.\n5\tSpeak with Ashâmi\tKanagir proved a true hunter. You and Ashâmi survived and should discuss a return to Urmâkh.\n",
[6803]="700375BD\n1\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tYou should speak with Reeve Fríthild before starting your attack.\n2\tDefeat the gate-guard and its minions\tDefeat the gate-guard and its minions.\n3\tDefeat Mabaj and his minions\tDefeat Mabaj and his minions.\n4\tDefeat Ushatar and his minions\tDefeat Ushatar and his minions.\n5\tDefeat Illska and his minions\tDefeat Illska and his minions.\n6\tEscape from Bardh-dorám through the postern gate\tEscape from Bardh-dorám through the postern gate.\n",
[6804]="70059A77\n1\tTalk to Bósi near the entrance to Clovengap\tBósi stands by the entrance to Clovengap.\n2\tExamine the warg corpse\tThe dwarves have discovered the corpse of a warg among the mist-laden grasses of Clovengap.\n3\tTalk to Bori by the warg corpse in Clovengap\tBori and the other dwarves gather around the warg corpse you found near the entrance to Clovengap.\n4\tExamine the corpse of the Angmarim cultist\tThe dwarves have discovered the corpse of an Angmarim cultist not far from the first body you encountered in Clovengap.\n5\tListen to the dwarves discuss the situation in Clovengap\tThe dwarves discuss the violence that has been done here in Clovengap; what does it mean for the safety of your travelling party?\n6\tTalk to Bósi in Clovengap\tThere are wolf-voices on the wind, and it seems the dwarves do not have long to prepare before the wargs attack!\n7\tRemain alert for the return of the wargs\tYou have fended off the wargs... for now.\n",
[6805]="70003270\n1\tSpeak to Avorthal\tAvorthal seeks Skorgrím Dourhand inside the goblin-infested vale of Rath Teraig. Avorthal has pledged the strength of his arm to your cause and seeks revenge upon Skorgrím for the harm he has caused the peoples of Ered Luin.\n2\tSpeak to Avorthal\tAvorthal seeks Skorgrím Dourhand inside the goblin-infested vale of Rath Teraig. A surprise attack by goblins has thinned the ranks of the Free Peoples in Rath Teraig, and now Avorthal leads a counterattack on the goblins lurking on the heights above.\n3\tSpeak to Avorthal\tAvorthal seeks Skorgrím Dourhand inside the goblin-infested vale of Rath Teraig. Avorthal has vowed to rescue Sara Oakheart, held captive by goblins within Rath Teraig, putting worries of his father's fate out of his mind.\n4\tSpeak to Avorthal\tSkorgrím Dourhand has escaped. Avorthal is waiting to speak with you regarding the course you should take next.\n",
[6806]="70028282\n1\tTalk to Elder Déin\tSpeak with Elder Déin.\n2\tListen to the Avanc-lûth\tListen to the Assembly. The people of Avanc-lûth have much to say.\n",
[6807]="70060585\n1\tTalk to Erlys\tYou should talk to Erlys before approaching Tornhad.\n2\tFollow Erlys\tYou should follow Erlys.\n3\tEavesdrop on Lagordal and the spy\tYou should stay hidden with Erlys and Igrain to eavesdrop. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tConfront Lagordal and the spy\tThe spy has noticed your presence. You should confront her and Lagordal with your allies.\n5\tDefend Erlys and Igrain\tThe confrontation has ended violently. You should defend Erlys and Igrain.\n6\tWait for Erlys to question Lagordal\tThe spy has been defeated, but Lagordal survives.\n7\tRelease Cariad from his bonds\tErlys has ordered you to release Cariad.\n8\tWait for further commands from Erlys\tYou should wait for further commands from Erlys.\n9\tTalk to the Ranger\tA Ranger has demanded to know the reason behind the Dunlendings' presence here. You should tell her what has happened.\n10\tWait for Lagordal's sentencing\tThere is still the question of Lagordal's fate.\n11\tTalk to Erlys\tYou have helped free Cariad and end Lagordal's scheming. You should talk to Erlys.\n",
[6808]="700253DA\n1\tTalk to Urcheneb\tYou are Iarvund, a soldier of the young Kingdom of Gondor, come to the Hill of Erech with your friend Urcheneb to serve your master Isildur.\n2\tTalk to Isildur\tIsildur is standing by the Stone of Erech, waiting to speak with you.\n3\tWait for the Men of the Mountain to arrive\tIsildur has asked you to look for the Men of the Mountain to arrive from the north slope of the hill of Erech. Isildur and his trusted soldiers have come to Erech and now wait for the arrival of the Men of the Mountain.\n4\tWitness the meeting between Isildur and the Men of the Mountain\tThe Men of the Mountain have arrived. Will they now swear the oath of allegiance to Isildur?\n5\tTalk to Britou\030Talk to Bodúan\030Talk to King Rioc\tThe King of the Mountain has sworn to fight against Sauron should he return to Middle-earth, and in return, his people will have the aid of Gondor.\n6\tTalk to Urcheneb\tUrcheneb and Isildur are on the summit of Erech.\n7\tListen to Candaith continue the telling of the tale\tMany years passed, and a shadow fell upon the Kingdom of Gondor.\n8\tTalk to Dorwë\tMany years passed, and a shadow fell upon the Kingdom of Gondor.\n9\tTalk to Isildur\tIt is as Isildur feared. Garth Lotheg has been besieged by Orcs, and its defenders slain.\n10\tExamine the disturbing idol erected by the Orcs in Garth Lotheg\tThe Orcs have erected a disturbing idol in the centre of Garth Lotheg.\n11\tTalk to Isildur\tIsildur is in the centre of Garth Lotheg, waiting to speak with you about the disturbing idol of Sauron the Orcs erected there.\n12\tListen to Candaith's story continue\tCandaith is continuing the story of Isildur and the oath of the Men of the Mountain.\n13\tTalk to Dorwë\tIsildur has returned to the Stone of Erech to summon the Men of the Mountain to fulfill their oath, but they have not yet arrived.\n14\tTalk to Isildur\tIsildur is at the summit by the Stone of Erech, waiting for the Men of the Mountain to arrive and fulfill their oath.\n15\tWait for the Men of the Mountain to arrive\tKing Rioc and the Men of the Mountain have come to Erech, summoned by Isildur to fulfill their oath.\n16\tSupport Isildur as he curses the Men of the Mountain for their refusal\tThe Men of the Mountain have arrived, but they refuse to honour the terms of their oath.\n17\tTalk to Isildur\tIsildur is at the summit of Erech.\n",
[6809]="70070223\n1\tTalk to Sigileth on the island of Kasukhín\tSigileth is eager to end the threat posed by Balakhâd and Nakási.\n2\tTalk to Balakhâd on the island of Kasukhín\tBalakhâd has expressed a desire to speak with you instead of fighting.\n3\tStand your ground against Balakhâd\tBalakhâd has attempted to convince you of the rightness of his position.\n4\tDefeat Balakhâd on the island of Kasukhín\tWords will not appease Balakhâd. Only combat will suffice!\n5\tDelay Nakási long enough for Cúridwan to finish her mission\tNakási has discovered your attempt to destroy the Song of Waves and Wind!\n6\tExamine Corudan's wound\tCorudan has been grievously injured by Nakási's deadly blade.\n",
[6810]="700253DC\n1\tTalk to Radanir on the path up to Zudrugund\tYou have come with Radanir to Zudrugund in pursuit of the uruk-band.\n2\tFight your way further up the path and talk to Candaith\tCandaith is further up the path to Zudrugund.\n3\tDefeat the Defender of the Span\tNúrzumgrat has left a mighty troll to defend the span below Zudrugund. It must be defeated if you are to reach the top.\n4\tFight your way up the path to Zudrugund and talk to Calenglad\tNow that the Defender of the Span is defeated, you can approach Zudrugund, where the leader of the uruks confronts the dwarves.\n5\tTalk to Nár outside Zudrugund\tNár is outside Zudrugund, and you should speak to him now that the uruks are defeated.\n",
[6811]="7003110A\n1\tTell Oldheart of the little bird's fate\tOldheart stands at the edge of his meadow in Fangorn. You should speak with Oldheart.\n2\tFollow Oldheart and defend yourself from enemies (total: 4)\tYou should follow Oldheart.\n3\tFollow Oldheart\tYou should follow Oldheart.\n4\tTalk to Oldheart\tYou should talk to Oldheart.\n5\tPick up the little bird\tThe dead bird can be found in the middle of the murky, foul pond.\n6\tBring the bird to Oldheart\tOldheart is at the pond's edge in Fangorn.\n7\tFollow Oldheart\tOldheart is in Fangorn.\n8\tSpeak with Oldheart, for the other Ents approach\tThe Ents are awake....\n",
[6812]="7005F559\n1\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. You have accompanied Hermáth Stormhammer and his warriors to confront the Iron Crown at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n2\tTalk to Spall\030Talk to Thrástan\tSpall and Thrástan can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. Despite all peril, Spall and Thrástan have accompanied you to Abkân'aban to confront the Iron Crown. You should talk to Spall and Thrástan.\n3\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. You have spoken to Spall and Thrástan and they intend to do what they can to repel the Iron Crown. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n4\tFight through the Iron Crown to the White Stone Forge atop Abkân'aban\tThe Iron Crown can be found at Abkân'aban. You should follow Hermáth Stormhammer and do what you can to repel the Iron Crown from the Stone of Wakening.\n5\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. You have fought your way to the White Stone Forge, but Allaban the Collector and his forces will soon arrive at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n6\tTalk to Thrástan\tThrástan can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. Although Allaban the Collector and the forces of the Iron Crown will soon arrive, Hermáth Stormhammer has asked you to escort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge. You should talk to Thrástan.\n7\tEscort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge\tThe White Stone Forge can be found atop Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. With sudden clarity, Thrástan wishes to return to the White Stone Forge. You should escort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge.\n8\tTalk to Thrástan\tThrástan can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. After escorting Thrástan to the White Stone Forge, it has sprung to life. You should talk to Thrástan.\n9\tWitness Thrástan's awakening\tThrástan can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. Thrástan has thanked you for your aid and asked you to bear witness to his \"awakening\". You should honour Thrástan's wishes.\n10\tTalk to the Forge-servant\tThe Forge-servant can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. By some ancient magic, Thrástan has been returned to his true form: the Forge-servant. You should talk to the Forge-servant.\n11\tConfront Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown\tAllaban the Collector and the Iron Crown can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown have arrived at Abkân'aban. You should confront them and prevent them from laying claim to the White Stone Forge.\n12\tWitness the wrath of the Forge-servant\tThe Forge-servant can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. The Forge-servant is confronting Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown. You should bear witness to the Forge-servant's wrath.\n13\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. The Forge-servant has used his ancient power to defeat Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[6813]="7006983A\n1\tTalk to Nauriel in the Citadel of Winds\tNauriel is within the great hall of the Citadel of Winds, ready to pursue Azagath and his allies.\n2\tTalk to Ushu in the Citadel of Winds\tUshu wants to speak to you in the Citadel of Winds.\n3\tFollow Ushu and Enât\tUshu has agreed to show you and Nauriel the passage through which Azagath and his allies fled.\n4\tTalk to Nauriel in the Citadel of Winds\tNauriel desires to chase after Azagath and his allies as they flee deeper into the Citadel of Winds.\n5\tTalk to Nauriel in the Citadel of Winds\tNauriel desires to chase after Azagath and his allies as they flee deeper into the Citadel of Winds.\n6\tTalk to Nauriel in the Citadel of Winds\tNauriel desires to chase after Azagath and his allies as they flee deeper into the Citadel of Winds.\n7\tTalk to Nauriel in the Citadel of Winds\tNauriel is waiting to speak with you within the Citadel of Winds.\n8\tFollow Azagath's trail through the door and outside the Citadel of Winds\tAzagath and his allies fled outside the Citadel of Winds by making use of the door at the bottom of the stairs.\n9\tTalk to Nauriel outside the Citadel of Winds\tNauriel has come with you outside the Citadel of Winds in pursuit of Azagath.\n10\tFollow Nauriel to the docks outside the Citadel of Winds\tAzagath and his allies have escaped from the island on which stands the Citadel of Winds.\n11\tTalk to the observant dock-worker outside the Citadel of Winds\tThe nearby dock-worker may know where Azagath and his allies fled.\n",
[6814]="70041324\n1\tTalk to Lothíriel\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. Balakhôr has sent a summons to Lothíriel to treat with him on his flagship, the Night-jewel.\n2\tTalk to Dorthaneth\tDorthaneth has come to the Great Hall of Dol Amroth to advise her friend Lothíriel.\n3\tGive Lothíriel your advice on her course of action\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. She has asked for your advice concerning Balakhôr's proposal that she treat with him on the deck of his flagship.\n4\tTalk to Dorthaneth\tDorthaneth is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. She has asked if you are willing to go to the Night-jewel in Lothíriel's stead.\n5\tTalk to Lothíriel and prepare to depart for the Night-jewel\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. You have agreed to meet with Balakhôr on his flagship, the Night-jewel, in Lothíriel's stead.\n6\tGo to the Night-jewel and meet with Balakhôr\tYou have come to the Night-jewel to treat with Balakhôr about the war.\n7\tTalk to Umer on the deck of the Night-jewel\tUmer, the Corsair emissary, has rowed you to the Night-jewel and is now ready to bring you to Balakhôr.\n8\tTalk to Balakhôr\tBalakhôr stands on the deck of the Night-jewel, waiting to hear why Lothíriel did not answer his summons.\n9\tTalk to Balakhôr\tYou are walking with Balakhôr on the deck of the Night-jewel, remaining alert for any sign of treachery.\n10\tBalakhôr has offered you a drink from his collection of wines.\t\n11\tTalk to Balakhôr\tBalakhôr is on the deck of the Night-jewel, and has more to say to you.\n12\tMake your own demands of Balakhôr\tBalakhôr has done enough talking. Now it is time for you to make your own demands of the Corsair leader.\n13\tBalakhôr has refused your demands, and instead has made you an offer: to step off the side of the Night-jewel and swim to shore.\t\n",
[6815]="7004DACF\n1\tTalk to King Thranduil\tKing Thranduil is standing in Torech Emel. You have come to Torech Emel to confront and defeat the Great Spider, Iphantemel. You should talk to King Thranduil.\n2\tFollow King Thranduil into Torech Emel\tKing Thranduil is at Torech Emel. King Thranduil intends to confront the Old Mother, but he is unnerved by the lack of spiders at Torech Emel. You should follow him and remain on guard.\n3\tListen to King Thranduil and his scout\tKing Thranduil's scout is speaking to him.\n4\tTalk to King Thranduil\tKing Thranduil is at Torech Emel. You have come to a webbed hollow in Torech Emel and learned that Iphantemel dwells in the nearby cavern. You should talk to King Thranduil.\n5\tRepel the spider ambush in Torech Emel\tYou are being attacked by Iphantemel's spiders in Torech Emel.\n6\tTalk to King Thranduil\tKing Thranduil is standing in the webbed hollow in Torech Emel. You have repelled an attack by the children of Iphantemel, but it seems the Old Mother may have called off her children.\n7\tConfront Iphantemel\tIphantemel can be found in a small cavern in Torech Emel. Iphantemel has called off her children and awaits King Thranduil.\n8\tTalk to King Thranduil\tKing Thranduil is at Torech Emel. After threatening King Thranduil, the bloated and sickly Iphantemel welcomed her own end. You should talk to King Thranduil.\n",
[6816]="7000D5B3\n1\tTalk to Forchon\tEnter Barad Tironn and speak to Forchon.\n2\tFind Laerdan\tEnter Barad Tironn and find Laerdan.\n3\tWait for Forchon in Barad Tironn\t\n",
})
